      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "χMT decreases from 58.55 cm3 K mol−1 at room temperature (0.1 T) to 38.14 cm3 K mol−1 at 2.0 K, close to the 59.99 cm3 K mol−1 expected for four DyIII and eight CuII. Magnetization at 2 and 5 K indicates anisotropy. ac susceptibility (2–12 K, 2.7 G, 1–1400 Hz) is frequency-dependent without maxima; a small dc field (0.01–0.1 T) does not change the ac profile. micro-SQUID magnetization of single crystals (0.04–0.6 K) shows temperature- and sweep-rate-dependent hysteresis, confirming SMM behavior attributed to the Dy4 core.",
