      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "χMT = 35.15 cm3 K mol−1 at room temperature (expected 35.13 for four GdIII and eight CuII). Upon cooling it rises to 37.11 cm3 K mol−1 at 10 K (0.1 T) then falls to 25.04 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K, indicating both ferro- and antiferromagnetic interactions. Fit of χT and magnetization with an isotropic Hamiltonian neglecting Cu–Cu coupling gives JGdGd = −0.15 cm−1, JCuGd = +0.5 cm−1, zJ = −0.019 cm−1, g = 2.10 (weak AF Gd–Gd and weak F Cu–Gd).",
